      "label": "Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-behavior",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 5059,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 3741,
      "label": "Map functions, roles and normal requests manually",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-artifacts",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 8925,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1448,
      "label": "Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-content",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 10498,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1352,
      "label": "Discover directories and files with controlled response filtering",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-vhosts",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 11975,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1352,
      "label": "Discover virtual hosts and hostname-selected applications",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-parameters",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 13452,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 2345,
      "label": "Map parameters, API methods, objects and writable properties",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:S12",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 15922,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 838,
      "label": "Map an authentication, session or multistep web flow",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "topic:web-mapping",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "# Map useful web behavior\n\nStart with a reachable URL. A suspicious parameter, hidden administration path or accepted account is not assumed.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:home",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "## Investigation flow\n\nMap useful web behavior\n\n · \n\nBranches describe evidence and missing conditions. Follow one useful lead, then return to unfinished coverage.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "## Capture a real request before fuzzing\n\nUse the browser/proxy to capture the real method, host, cookie and input; curl is the replay baseline.\n\n```bash\ncurl -skD headers.txt -o body.html http://TARGET:PORT/\ncurl -skI https://TARGET:PORT/\n```\n\n**Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-0-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Redirect to a different hostname\n\nResolve and replay that hostname before testing paths.\n\n**Discover virtual hosts and hostname-selected applications — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-0-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 845,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A login, upload or object endpoint\n\nCapture its normal authenticated request and available roles.\n\n**Map parameters, API methods, objects and writable properties — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-0-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nEvery request reaches the wrong/default site: fix the host/scheme/session first.\n\n**Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 1250,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "## Discover paths with Gobuster or the documented ffuf variant\n\nFirst request a missing path to learn the false-positive body/status/length. Keep the correct host and session.\n\n```bash\ngobuster dir -u http://TARGET:PORT/ -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt -t 10 -o gobuster-root.txt\n```\n\n**Discover directories and files with controlled response filtering — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-1-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1250,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A backup, config, source or repository path\n\nRead its content; a 200 response alone does not establish an artifact.\n\n**Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-1-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1475,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A new application function\n\nMap its parameters and authorization boundary.\n\n**Map parameters, API methods, objects and writable properties — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-1-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 1250,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nAll candidates look identical: repair the response controls rather than collecting more false positives.\n\n**Discover directories and files with controlled response filtering — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## Enumerate hostname-selected sites\n\nUse this when DNS, certificates, redirects or page content suggest another hostname.\n\n```bash\ngobuster vhost -u http://DOMAIN:PORT/ --append-domain -w /usr/share/seclists/Discovery/DNS/subdomains-top1million-5000.txt -o vhosts.txt\n```\n\n**Discover virtual hosts and hostname-selected applications — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-2-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A host has a distinct response\n\nBrowse it with the correct Host header and repeat function/path mapping.\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-mapping:check-2-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 1880,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nNo distinct host: return to real application functions and exposed scripts.\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "notes:web-mapping",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/web-mapping.md",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2410,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 850
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-label:web-mapping",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2350,
      "y": 2410,
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Full procedures and alternatives\n\nThe adjacent embedded note is readable here. Scroll inside it for complete variants. Commands and decisions continue below.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 3685,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state\n\nAn HTTP endpoint, redirect or hostname-dependent response",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 3645,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -skD headers.txt -o body.html http://TARGET:PORT/\ncurl -skI https://TARGET:PORT/\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3625,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe hostname/scheme redirect identifies the application request context to reproduce.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3871,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm the hostname routes to the assigned address and preserve its TLS/Host/session state.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3575,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe correct named request reaches a distinct application: map its functions.\n\n**Verify:** Record final URL, host, status, redirects, cookies and authentication context before comparing payload results.\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-identity|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3892,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe candidate name produces only the default missing-host response: discard that virtual-host inference.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 4113,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nRedirect loops can mean missing cookies/host routing; repair the normal request before testing vulnerabilities.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3575,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncurl -skL -D headers.txt -o body.html http://TARGET:PORT/\ncurl -sk -o /dev/null -w 'code=%{http_code} bytes=%{size_download} type=%{content_type} redirect=%{redirect_url}\\n' http://TARGET:PORT/\n```\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-identity|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3941,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Discover virtual hosts and hostname-selected applications\n\n**When:** DNS names, redirects, certificate names or a default virtual-host response\n\n**Still required:** A destination listener, relevant domain candidates and controlled Host/SNI routing\n\n**Discover virtual hosts and hostname-selected applications — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4272,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\n**When:** Forms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces\n\n**Still required:** A normal request baseline and the relevant account/role; authorized accounts for role comparisons\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-identity:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4603,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts\n\n**When:** JavaScript endpoints, backup names, exposed configuration or Git metadata\n\n**Still required:** Readable application artifact or a complete recoverable repository; preserve the public-source scope\n\n**Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 5234,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\nForms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 5194,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -b cookies.txt -D response-headers.txt http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 5174,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe normal request exposes a file-selecting input discovered through functionality, not guessed from a payload list.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 5420,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nFind the actual input semantics, account/role and normal response before file/read/authorization tests.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 5124,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nControlled comparisons prove a useful primitive: choose its method and remaining checks.\n\n**Verify:** Retain method, route, input location, identity and expected normal behavior; do not infer vulnerability from an interesting parameter name.\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-behavior|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 5465,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe parameter only selects an allowlisted public report: discard unrestricted-path inference.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 5686,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nUnknown ownership or an expired session prevents interpreting differences; re-establish the baseline.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5124,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nMETHOD PATH | CONTENT-TYPE | ACCESS CONTEXT/ROLE\nINPUT LOCATION + NAME | BASELINE VALUE\nSTATUS | LENGTH/HASH | REDIRECT | MARKER/ERROR/TIME\nOBJECT/FUNCTION SELECTED | NEXT ONE-VARIABLE TEST\n```\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-behavior|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5514,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Cross an object-ownership boundary\n\n**When:** A request selects an object by ID/path and two authorized ownership contexts are available\n\n**Still required:** The server accepts a lower-privilege identity's request for an object it should not access\n\n**Cross an object-ownership boundary — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5845,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Read files through directory traversal\n\n**When:** A download/path parameter or URL segment influences a local filename\n\n**Still required:** Untrusted path reaches a filesystem read outside its intended directory; process identity can read the requested file\n\n**Read files through directory traversal — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6176,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish upload acceptance, storage and retrieval\n\n**When:** An upload/import/attachment function\n\n**Still required:** A valid upload request and permitted account; the server accepts and stores controlled bytes\n\n**Establish upload acceptance, storage and retrieval — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6483,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Prove server-side template evaluation and identify its engine\n\n**When:** Controlled input appears in a server-rendered template, preview, email or report\n\n**Still required:** The application evaluates attacker-controlled template syntax and the selected engine exposes a useful object or function\n\n**Prove server-side template evaluation and identify its engine — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6814,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use an XML parser's external-entity behavior for bounded file read\n\n**When:** A working XML request reaches a server-side parser that accepts a controlled document or field\n\n**Still required:** External entity or XInclude processing is enabled and the parser identity can read the selected file\n\n**Use an XML parser's external-entity behavior for bounded file read — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7145,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Test structured NoSQL operator injection with identity controls\n\n**When:** A login or search accepts JSON/nested form properties and evidence suggests an operator-based document query\n\n**Still required:** The framework preserves an attacker-controlled operator object and the query uses it without rejecting its type\n\n**Test structured NoSQL operator injection with identity controls — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7476,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match PHP deserialization gadgets to installed dependencies\n\n**When:** Source or request evidence shows controlled serialized PHP data reaches unsafe unserialize\n\n**Still required:** Required gadget classes and compatible dependency versions are loaded; transport preserves exact serialized bytes\n\n**Match PHP deserialization gadgets to installed dependencies — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7807,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate unsafe YAML object construction\n\n**When:** Source or errors identify server-side Python YAML loading of controlled content\n\n**Still required:** The application uses an unsafe PyYAML loader that permits the selected Python object constructor\n\n**Validate unsafe YAML object construction — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8138,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Test Shellshock only through a confirmed CGI-to-Bash chain\n\n**When:** A real CGI endpoint invokes Bash and component/patch evidence supports the vulnerable family\n\n**Still required:** HTTP-derived environment data reaches an affected Bash process and the selected command is available\n\n**Test Shellshock only through a confirmed CGI-to-Bash chain — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-behavior:next-9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8469,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Discover directories and files with controlled response filtering\n\n**When:** An application has unlinked paths, backups or administration endpoints\n\n**Still required:** Correct base URL/session and a measured nonexistent-path response; bounded relevant wordlist\n\n**Discover directories and files with controlled response filtering — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 9100,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts\n\nJavaScript endpoints, backup names, exposed configuration or Git metadata",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 9060,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk http://TARGET:PORT/robots.txt\ncurl -sk http://TARGET:PORT/.git/HEAD\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 9040,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe path and Git reference are investigation leads; neither proves a working secret or complete repository.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 9286,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCompare missing-path controls, retrieve actual permitted artifacts and verify recovered history/account context.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 8990,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nRelevant source/history is recoverable and exposes a typed artifact: inspect it through the credential workflow.\n\n**Verify:** Confirm actual file/history content and distinguish a historical secret from a usable current credential.\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-artifacts|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 9331,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe same body is returned for arbitrary missing paths: reject the apparent metadata exposure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 9552,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nHEAD without objects leaves repository recovery incomplete; document available content instead of inventing history.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8990,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncurl -sk http://TARGET:PORT/robots.txt\ncurl -sk http://TARGET:PORT/sitemap.xml\ncurl -sk http://TARGET:PORT/.git/HEAD\ncurl -sk http://TARGET:PORT/openapi.json\ncurl -sk http://TARGET:PORT/swagger.json\n```\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-artifacts|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9404,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9735,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration\n\n**When:** A product/version clue, advisory or component-specific public PoC\n\n**Still required:** Exact vulnerable build/configuration, required access and endpoint behavior; reviewable source and a verifiable expected effect\n\n[[tracks/04 Public Exploits.canvas|Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration → 04 Public Exploits]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-artifacts:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10042,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map parameters, API methods, objects and writable properties\n\n**When:** An API/schema, numeric object IDs, hidden fields or different HTTP methods\n\n**Still required:** A valid request and explicit role/object ownership; exact input format and content type\n\n**Map parameters, API methods, objects and writable properties — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 10673,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Discover directories and files with controlled response filtering\n\nAn application has unlinked paths, backups or administration endpoints",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 10633,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -D - http://TARGET:PORT/KNOWN_MISSING_PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 10613,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe candidate's actual function differs from the soft-404 control despite equal status codes.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 10859,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nRequest a known-missing path under the same host/session and compare status, body and length. Open each distinct Gobuster/ffuf result; a uniform login page or soft-404 is a filter problem, not a directory finding.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 10563,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nIndependent retrieval confirms an actual function: add its request to the behavior map.\n\n**Verify:** Open candidates and record their actual behavior; status/length alone is only a selection clue.\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-content|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 10904,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe candidate matches the wildcard error body: remove it from the useful queue.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 11125,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nRate limiting or session expiry distorts response size; restore stable controls before filtering.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10563,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ngobuster dir -u http://TARGET:PORT/ -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt -t 10 -o gobuster-root.txt\n```\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-content|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10881,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\n**When:** Forms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces\n\n**Still required:** A normal request baseline and the relevant account/role; authorized accounts for role comparisons\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11212,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts\n\n**When:** JavaScript endpoints, backup names, exposed configuration or Git metadata\n\n**Still required:** Readable application artifact or a complete recoverable repository; preserve the public-source scope\n\n**Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-content:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11543,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish upload acceptance, storage and retrieval\n\n**When:** An upload/import/attachment function\n\n**Still required:** A valid upload request and permitted account; the server accepts and stores controlled bytes\n\n**Establish upload acceptance, storage and retrieval — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 12150,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Discover virtual hosts and hostname-selected applications\n\nDNS names, redirects, certificate names or a default virtual-host response",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 12110,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk --resolve HOSTNAME:PORT:TARGET https://HOSTNAME:PORT/\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 12090,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA reproducible hostname-selected application is a new mapping target on the same address.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 12336,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nSend a random Host header as a negative control, compare the candidate's real response, then browse it with the correct hostname. A different status caused only by redirects or a default site is not a confirmed vhost.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 12040,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe named application has distinct verified behavior: give it its own session/function map.\n\n**Verify:** Compare candidate and nonexistent-host responses, including content and redirects; resolve to the intended scoped address.\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-vhosts|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 12381,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nAll candidate hosts receive the same default body: discard the claimed distinct application.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 12602,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nTLS routing or local DNS is wrong: fix that context before deciding a vhost is absent.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12040,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ngobuster vhost -u http://DOMAIN:PORT/ --append-domain -w /usr/share/seclists/Discovery/DNS/subdomains-top1million-5000.txt -o vhosts.txt\n```\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-vhosts|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12382,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state\n\n**When:** An HTTP endpoint, redirect or hostname-dependent response\n\n**Still required:** Correct scheme/port and virtual host; saved cookies/headers for authenticated comparisons\n\n**Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12689,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\n**When:** Forms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces\n\n**Still required:** A normal request baseline and the relevant account/role; authorized accounts for role comparisons\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-vhosts:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13020,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Expand names through DNS records and zone transfers\n\n**When:** A DNS server, domain name or host aliases\n\n**Still required:** Reachable DNS transport and relevant authoritative zone; AXFR requires an allowed TCP zone transfer\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Expand names through DNS records and zone transfers → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 13627,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Map parameters, API methods, objects and writable properties\n\nAn API/schema, numeric object IDs, hidden fields or different HTTP methods",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 13587,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -i -b cookies.txt http://TARGET:PORT/api/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 13567,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe actual object, method and writable input are known; returned owner/role fields are only candidate security boundaries.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 13813,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nDetermine field binding, ownership, persistence and server authorization with controlled accounts.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 13517,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA protected field/action changes under a lower role and is independently verified: select its authorization method.\n\n**Verify:** Prove which input is consumed and whether state changes persist in an independent read.\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-parameters|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 13858,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe server ignores the sensitive field and privileges remain unchanged: reject that assignment hypothesis.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 14079,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nMalformed JSON or wrong content type makes a failed request inconclusive; reproduce the valid update first.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13517,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nffuf -w /usr/share/seclists/Discovery/Web-Content/burp-parameter-names.txt -u 'http://TARGET:PORT/PATH?FUZZ=test' -ac -o params-get.json\n```\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#web-parameters|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13859,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Modify a protected property through excessive writable fields\n\n**When:** API objects expose role, ownership or security-sensitive properties\n\n**Still required:** The server binds an untrusted property to a persistent security-relevant field without checking permission\n\n**Modify a protected property through excessive writable fields — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14166,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Cross an object-ownership boundary\n\n**When:** A request selects an object by ID/path and two authorized ownership contexts are available\n\n**Still required:** The server accepts a lower-privilege identity's request for an object it should not access\n\n**Cross an object-ownership boundary — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14497,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Prove visible or blind operating-system command injection\n\n**When:** An input appears in a command-like operation or causes shell-dependent behavior\n\n**Still required:** Input reaches command execution with an exploitable parsing boundary; process identity/runtime can perform the selected proof\n\n**Prove visible or blind operating-system command injection — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14828,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish SQL query influence and DBMS context\n\n**When:** Database errors or controlled true/false response differences\n\n**Still required:** Input reaches a SQL query; a valid request and stable response baseline exist\n\n**Establish SQL query influence and DBMS context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:next-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15135,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Execute browser code and validate a useful same-origin action\n\n**When:** Untrusted input reaches an executable HTML/JavaScript context\n\n**Still required:** Payload reaches a browser execution sink; any useful privileged action additionally needs a victim context, same-origin access and a valid request state\n\n**Execute browser code and validate a useful same-origin action — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-parameters:next-5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15466,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use server-side requests to inspect reachable internal behavior\n\n**When:** URL import, preview, webhook or fetch behavior\n\n**Still required:** The application server performs a controllable request; destination/protocol policy and its network position permit the selected resource\n\n**Use server-side requests to inspect reachable internal behavior — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S12:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 16097,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Map an authentication, session or multistep web flow\n\nthe application exposes login, registration, recovery, role change, state-changing business action, authenticated API or another session-dependent flow.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S12:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 16057,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S12:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 16037,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\ncapture a working anonymous and/or authenticated request, then record method, scheme/host/path, headers, cookies/tokens, body fields, hidden values, redirects, role and each step required to complete the action. Include non-GET/POST methods, JSON/XML bodies and WebSocket/API messages when the application actually uses them.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S12:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 16355,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nreplay the unchanged request first; then change one identity, object, property or session boundary at a time. Confirm freshness, CSRF/token coupling, object ownership and whether the result is server-side rather than a browser-only presentation change.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S12:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15987,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\ncontrolled unauthorized effect → D14 or the matching primitive; invariant authorization/ownership enforcement → ruled out for that transition; token expiry, cache, redirect or client-side behavior masks the result → inconclusive/D31.\n\n**Verify:** preserve one reproducible request/response pair and the exact role/session/object delta. Mapping a field or flow is not itself exploitation.\n\n[[notes/web-mapping.md#S12|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S12:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16376,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S12:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16573,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
